        "id": 1003935
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-02-19T12:19:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It\u0027s a bit weird that if this permssion is blocked or not a assigned for a user that there may still be change messages from that user, which may look unexpected (e.g. if the user has the Rebase permission, they can rebase the change which adds change messages). Are we fine with this? If yes, should we document this?\n\nAlternatively, should having the Review permission rather be a pre-condition for any write action, similarly to how the Read permission is a pre-condition for any action? This way when there is spammer we only need to block the Review permission, instead of needing to block all kind of other permissions that are assigned to Registered Users as well (Rebase, Revert, voting on Code-Review, etc.).\n\nI\u0027m also interested what the others think about this?\n@matthias.sohn@gmail.com @nasser.grainawi@oss.qualcomm.com",
      "revId": "852ff5001f423048dee1f791a3e6c3b39dfc08d7",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
